.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
.TH ATL\-DOCTOR 1 "November 2026" "atl-doctor 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
atl-doctor \- find out why an Android app does not run correctly under Android Translation Layer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B atl-doctor record
[\fB\-o\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-android\fR] [\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIDIR\fR | \fB\-\-launcher\fR \fICMD\fR]
[\fB\-\-atl\-src\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-headless\fR] [\fB\-\-steps\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-trace\fR] [\fB\-\-light\fR] [\fB\-\-heap\fR] [\fB\-\-input\fR]
\fIAPK\fR [\fB\-\-\fR \fIATL\-ARGS\fR]
.br
.B atl-doctor pack
[\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-full\fR] [\fB\-\-user\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-host\fR \fINAME\fR] \fIDIR\fR
.br
.B atl-doctor mark
[\fB\-d\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fITEXT\fR]
.br
.B atl-doctor report
[\fB\-f\fR \fItext\fR|\fIjson\fR|\fIhtml\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fICLASS\fR[,\fICLASS\fR]]
[\fB\-\-log\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-atl\-src\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-aosp\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-density\fR \fID\fR] [\fB\-\-jank\-min\-frames\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fIDIR\fR [\fIANDROID\-DIR\fR]]
.br
.B atl-doctor diff
[\fB\-f\fR \fItext\fR|\fIjson\fR] [\fB\-\-fail\-on\fR \fInew\fR|\fICLASS\fR[,\fICLASS\fR]] \fIOLD.json\fR \fINEW.json\fR
.br
.B atl-doctor explain
\fB\-d\fR \fIDIR\fR [\fB\-\-aosp\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-jank\-min\-frames\fR \fIN\fR] \fIID\fR
.br
.B atl-doctor check
[\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-atl\-src\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-aosp\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-android\fR]
.br
.B atl-doctor scan
[\fB\-f\fR \fItext\fR|\fIjson\fR|\fIhtml\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-atl\-src\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB\-\-compare\-src\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-aosp\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-sdk\-int\fR \fIN\fR] \fIAPK\fR...
.br
.B atl-doctor compare
[\fB\-o\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-scenario\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fIDIR\fR | \fB\-\-launcher\fR \fICMD\fR] [\fB\-\-atl\-src\fR \fIDIR\fR]
[\fB\-\-deep\fR] [\fB\-\-atl\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR \fB\-\-android\-dir\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-density\fR \fID\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-aosp\-fetch\fR]
\fIAPK\fR [\fB\-\-\fR \fIATL\-ARGS\fR]
.br
.B atl-doctor state
\fBsave\fR|\fBload\fR [\fB\-\-android\fR] [\fB\-\-launcher\fR \fICMD\fR] \fIAPK\fR \fINAME\fR
.br
.B atl-doctor scenario-from
[\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR] \fIRECORDING\fR
.PP
.B atl-doctor
[\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.PP
Every command also takes \fB\-q\fR (\fB\-\-quiet\fR), \fB\-v\fR (\fB\-\-verbose\fR)
and \fB\-h\fR (\fB\-\-help\fR).
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B atl-doctor
records an app under Android Translation Layer (ATL) and, if asked, on an Android device, and reports what
is most worth fixing in ATL: stubs that were hit, missing methods, swallowed exceptions, differences in the
view tree, slow frames, hangs and memory growth.
With a screenshot per mark it also finds rendering defects on ATL (class render): text whose colour is
hardly distinguishable from the background (WCAG contrast under 4.5:1, large text 3:1, measured in the picture),
text, icons or selected tabs that are one flat colour, and views that stick out of their window or parent.
Truncated text is not checked (the view tree has no text metrics). In a comparison with Android a defect that Android shows as well is dropped.
Findings are ranked by what to fix first and carry a stable ID, so two reports can be compared with
.BR "atl-doctor diff" .
.PP
A hit stub whose AOSP method is just as trivial (same empty body, same returned value or the parameter
returned unchanged, e.g. \fBView.isInEditMode\fR returning false) is not a gap in ATL: it is marked "like AOSP"
(\fBdetails.like_aosp\fR in json), left out of "Hit stubs" and "Fix first" and listed once under "Notes".
The comparison always reads real AOSP source: the tree given with \fB\-\-aosp\fR (or $ATL_DOCTOR_AOSP) or, without one,
a tree that atl\-doctor fetches itself. It clones only the \fBjava/\fR directories (no tests) of
platform/frameworks/base from android.googlesource.com (shallow, \fB\-\-filter=blob:none\fR, sparse) at the newest
release tag of Android 14 (API 34; a missing series falls back to the next lower one) into
\fI$XDG_CACHE_HOME/atl\-doctor/aosp/<tag>\fR (default \fI~/.cache\fR), once; later runs use the cache offline.
$ATL_DOCTOR_AOSP_URL replaces the repository URL (a mirror). Without network and without a cache, or with
\fB\-\-no\-aosp\-fetch\fR, the report says "AOSP comparison not possible" in its environment section and the stub hits
stay unfiltered; nothing is dropped silently.
.PP
The agent sets breakpoints in System.exit, Runtime.exit and Runtime.halt (agent option \fBnoexit\fR turns that off).
The report's \fBExit cause\fR section then names the first call: the exit status, the calling app frame, the thread,
the stack and the last five exceptions before it. If the process ended without such a call, the finding says
"Ended without a System.exit/Runtime.exit call being seen" and gives the process's exit status or signal.
.PP
When a \fBclose\-window\fR step ran, \fBrecord\fR measures whether ATL's process ends within 5 s. The environment
section always has the line "Ends after window close": "yes (1.2 s)", "no (still running after 5 s)" or "not checked"
(no close-window step, or the run was stopped first). Below it the exit status or signal and the processes of ATL's
own session (PID and name only) are listed. "no" is a finding of class \fBlifecycle\fR (weight 60, like a crash).
.PP
At every mark the agent asks the system what the app would be told (agent option \fBnosys\fR turns that off): the
active network and its transports and capabilities, the active NetworkInfo, a fixed list of PackageManager features
and packages (present or not), the display size and density, and the number of accounts (never their names).
It asks through the Application itself; the app's own calls are not recorded. It also sets breakpoints in
registerReceiver and in every BroadcastReceiver.onReceive and writes the actions registered and delivered.
The report \fBBroadcasts registered, never delivered\fR names each sticky action (one Android delivers on registration) a receiver waits for that never came
(this works without an Android recording; against one it says whether Android delivered it), and with
.B report DIR ANDROID\-DIR
the section \fBSystem answers differ\fR lists the queries whose last answer differs between ATL and Android.
The Android agent is the same source; without a rooted device and the agent built for it that side has no answers
and the report says so.
.PP
Results go to standard output, messages to standard error.
The tool never asks questions and never opens a browser.
If an optional probe is missing, one line on standard error says so and the recording goes on without it;
.B atl-doctor check
lists what is missing and how to add it.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B record
Run \fIAPK\fR under ATL until it ends or until SIGINT, and write a capture directory.
Arguments after \fB\-\-\fR go to android\-translation\-layer.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIDIR\fR"
Capture directory (default: \fI./atl\-doctor\-YYYYmmdd\-HHMMSS\fR, with \fB\-android\fR appended for \fB\-\-android\fR).
It must not exist or must be empty.
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix " DIR"
ATL installation prefix (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_PREFIX).
.TP
.BI \-\-launcher " CMD"
Start ATL with the command \fICMD\fR (split like a shell would, not run by one) instead of
\fIPREFIX\fR/bin/android\-translation\-layer, for example an ATL that is packaged as a Flatpak:
\fB\-\-launcher \(aqflatpak run \-\-user ID\(aq\fR.
\fIAPK\fR and the ATL arguments are appended; the launcher must pass them on to ATL.
Excludes \fB\-\-prefix\fR.
Without a prefix, what needs one is not available: the JVMTI agent (frame times, hangs, \fBwait\-idle\fR)
and the stub list from ATL's jars.
View trees (\fBclick "Text"\fR, \fBclick id/\fR\fINAME\fR, \fBclick\fR \fIX\fR,\fIY\fR from the content origin,
scroll distances, window images) are asked of ATL at run time; an ATL without ATLViewDump never answers,
and \fBclick\fR then fails instead of counting from the window frame.
There is no \fImemory.tsv\fR, because the launcher's own process is not the app.
The app must see the APK and the capture directory (method trace, wheel log, view trees) under the same
path (Flatpak: \fB\-\-filesystem=\fR\fIDIR\fR). The environment atl\-doctor sets goes to the launcher;
a launcher that drops \fBLD_PRELOAD\fR (as \fBflatpak run\fR does) must pass the wheel shim on itself
(Flatpak: \fB\-\-env=LD_PRELOAD=\fR\fIPATH\fR, path visible in the sandbox), otherwise \fBscroll\fR \fIN\fR
scrolls smoothly.
.TP
.BI \-\-atl\-src " DIR"
ATL source tree; used to build the list of stubs that are watched (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_ATL_SRC).
.TP
.BI \-\-agent " PATH"
JVMTI agent library (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_AGENT, then the helper directories).
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run ATL in a private invisible KWin session (kwin_wayland \-\-virtual); needed for screenshots.
.TP
.BI \-\-steps " FILE"
Drive the app with a step file. Implies \fB\-\-headless\fR under ATL.
Per step the capture records the time, the number of frames drawn and the distance scrolled (\fIsteps.tsv\fR).
A \fBwait\-window\fR step ends in \fIsteps.tsv\fR at the time the window appeared (under ATL, from KWin's own clock),
not when the step noticed it. Only a window that is there when the step begins or appears while it waits counts;
one that came and went earlier does not.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-trace
No method trace. The trace slows the app down many times over (a first start can take minutes); without it
the times in \fIsteps.tsv\fR are realistic, but the report has no stub hits.
.TP
.B \-\-light
Fast recording that keeps the app at (almost) its normal speed: the agent is attached once the runtime runs
(ATL \fB\-\-attach\-agent\fR; the runtime stays non\-debuggable), ATL counts calls of its stub methods itself
(\fBATL_STUB_HITS\fR, \fIstubhits.tsv\fR) and the time line comes from ART's sampling profiler (every 1 ms) instead
of a full method trace; the report shows the busiest methods per phase. Needs an ATL that has both.
.TP
.B \-\-heap
Count instances and bytes per class at every mark (agent; slow, forces a garbage collection per mark).
.TP
.B \-\-android
Record the same app on an Android device over adb instead (own capture directory).
.TP
.B \-\-input
With \fB\-\-android\fR: also record what is done on the device (touches and keys, \fBgetevent\fR; targets from
\fBuiautomator dump\fR) into \fIinput.jsonl\fR. Costs some speed (a dump loop runs). Under ATL \fIinput.jsonl\fR is written from the
agent whenever views were clicked, with or without this option.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Only errors on standard error.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
More messages on standard error (for \fBrecord\fR: the helpers found and the ATL command line).
.RE
.TP
.B mark
Start a new phase in the running recording (through the control FIFO of the capture directory).
Without \fITEXT\fR the phase is called "mark N".
.RS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Capture directory (default: the newest \fI./atl\-doctor\-*\fR).
.RE
.TP
.B pack
Pack a capture directory into one \fI.tar.gz\fR that can be handed on, and print its path. Cleaned (default): paths
(\fI$HOME\fR becomes ~), user and host name, private IP addresses (\fI<lan\-ip\-N>\fR), public ones (\fI<ip\-N>\fR), MAC
addresses, tokens, Authorization/Cookie headers, URL parameters such as token, key, password and sid, e\-mail and account
names become placeholders (the same value always gets the same number); the text typed into input fields is removed.
Left out in both stages: files that \fBreport\fR does not read, empty files and duplicates. \fISANITIZED.txt\fR in the
archive lists the rules, the number of replacements per rule and the files left out, never the original values.
The archive is named \fIPACKAGE\-DATE\-TIME.tar.gz\fR, with \fB\-\-full\fR \fIPACKAGE\-DATE\-TIME\-FULL.tar.gz\fR.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Archive to write (default: next to \fIDIR\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-full
Do not clean: all data as recorded, including passwords. Only for people you trust.
.TP
.BI \-\-user " NAME"
.TQ
.BI \-\-home " DIR"
.TQ
.BI \-\-host " NAME"
User name, home directory and host name to replace (default: current user, \fI$HOME\fR, this machine). Needed when
the recording comes from another machine; a /home/\fINAME\fR in the data is found anyway.
.RE
.TP
.B report
Report from a capture directory; with a second directory (an Android capture) ATL against Android, phases and
steps paired by name and number. With \fB\-\-log\fR a log file is evaluated instead.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fItext\fR|\fIjson\fR|\fIhtml\fR"
Output format (default: text). \fBhtml\fR needs \fB\-o\fR.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write to \fIFILE\fR instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on " CLASS" [, CLASS ]
Exit with status 4 if a finding of one of these classes exists.
Classes: crash, missing, exception\-atl\-only, stub\-result\-used, tree\-visible, render, memory\-growth, jank, other.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " FILE"
Log mode: one log file per phase (repeatable).
Lines of the agent's output that a launcher appended to the log, each after the prefix
.RB \(lq "# atl\-doctor\-agent: " \(rq,
give the exceptions with their stack and the agent's problems.
.TP
.BI \-\-atl\-src " DIR"
ATL source tree; matches logged stub messages against its stub list (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_ATL_SRC).
.TP
.BI \-\-aosp " DIR"
AOSP source tree (root or frameworks/base) to compare stubs and missing methods with (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_AOSP).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-aosp\-fetch
Do not download AOSP source when \fB\-\-aosp\fR is not given (default: fetch once into the cache, see DESCRIPTION).
.TP
.BI \-\-density " D"
Android display density for the tree comparison (default: from the Android capture).
.TP
.BI \-\-jank\-min\-frames " N"
Fewest frames a phase needs for a jank finding (default: 30). A phase that is slow but has fewer frames gets no
finding; the report notes it as \(lqtoo few frames\(rq instead.
.RE
.TP
.B diff
Compare two JSON reports: each finding ID is new, gone, changed or unchanged.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fItext\fR|\fIjson\fR"
Output format (default: text).
.TP
.BI \-\-fail\-on " new" | CLASS [, CLASS ]
Exit with status 4 if there are new findings (\fBnew\fR) or new findings of these classes.
.RE
.TP
.B explain
Everything known about one finding: occurrences, stack, details, AOSP comparison, images.
\fIID\fR is a full ID, a short ID or a unique prefix of one.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir " \fIDIR\fR"
Capture directory or JSON report (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-aosp " DIR"
AOSP source tree (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_AOSP).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-aosp\-fetch
Do not download AOSP source when \fB\-\-aosp\fR is not given (default: fetch once into the cache, see DESCRIPTION).
.TP
.BI \-\-jank\-min\-frames " N"
Fewest frames a phase needs for a jank finding (default: 30). A phase that is slow but has fewer frames gets no
finding; the report notes it as \(lqtoo few frames\(rq instead.
.RE
.TP
.B check
Check the environment and say, per probe, whether it is available, why not, and how to add it.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix " DIR"
ATL installation prefix (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_PREFIX).
.TP
.BI \-\-atl\-src " DIR"
ATL source tree (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_ATL_SRC).
.TP
.BI \-\-aosp " DIR"
AOSP source tree (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_AOSP).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-aosp\-fetch
Do not download AOSP source when \fB\-\-aosp\fR is not given (default: fetch once into the cache, see DESCRIPTION).
.TP
.B \-\-android
Also check adb and the Android device.
.RE
.TP
.B scan
Static coverage of one or more APKs against ATL, without starting them.
Exit status 1 if an APK had to be skipped.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " \fItext\fR|\fIjson\fR|\fIhtml\fR"
Output format (default: text). \fBhtml\fR needs \fB\-o\fR.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write to \fIFILE\fR instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-atl\-src " DIR"
ATL source tree (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_ATL_SRC).
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix " DIR"
ATL installation prefix (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_PREFIX).
.TP
.BI \-\-compare\-src " DIR"
Second ATL source tree (with build*/api\-impl.jar) to compare.
.TP
.BI \-\-aosp " DIR"
AOSP source tree (root or frameworks/base) to compare stubs and missing methods with (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_AOSP).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-aosp\-fetch
Do not download AOSP source when \fB\-\-aosp\fR is not given (default: fetch once into the cache, see DESCRIPTION).
.TP
.BI \-\-sdk\-int " N"
SDK_INT that ATL reports (default: the app's minSdk, at least 9).
.RE
.TP
.B compare
Record the same scenario under ATL and on Android (\fBrecord\fR and \fBrecord \-\-android\fR into
\fIDIR\fR/atl and \fIDIR\fR/android) and write a short comparison to \fIDIR\fR/report.md (at most 60 lines, also on
standard output) and \fIDIR\fR/report.json: likely causes first (crash, exception only on ATL through app code,
lifecycle difference, native library or symbol missing, missing method, exception only on ATL inside the platform,
stub whose result is used, EGL/audio error, other stubs, screenshots that differ; a candidate first seen while
the app starts, before the first mark, ranks lower), then stubs hit by count with their caller, exceptions only on ATL, lifecycle
differences, missing native pieces and the screenshots of each step compared (worst first; diff pictures in
\fIDIR\fR/shots). It only shows; nothing is changed.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIDIR\fR"
Output directory (default: ./atl\-doctor\-compare\-<time>).
.TP
.BI \-\-scenario " FILE"
Step file for both sides (default: wait 15 s, then one screenshot).
.TP
.BI \-\-prefix " DIR"
ATL installation prefix (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_PREFIX).
.TP
.BI \-\-launcher " CMD"
Start ATL with \fICMD\fR instead, as for \fBrecord\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-atl\-src " DIR"
ATL source tree for the stub list (default: $ATL_DOCTOR_ATL_SRC).
.TP
.B \-\-deep
Record ATL with the full method trace and the agent from the start. Without it the recording is light
(\fBrecord \-\-light\fR): the runtime is not made debuggable, because that forces the interpreter and changes
the timing.
.TP
.BI \-\-atl\-dir " DIR"
.TQ
.BI \-\-android\-dir " DIR"
Compare these two captures instead of recording.
.TP
.BI \-\-density " D"
Android screen density (default: from the Android capture).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-aosp\-fetch
Do not download AOSP source (see \fBreport\fR).
.RE
.TP
.B scenario-from
Make a step file from a recorded input: \fIRECORDING\fR is a capture directory with \fIinput.jsonl\fR or that file itself.
The step file replays every tap, long tap, text, key, scroll and back with \fBtap\fR and \fBlong\-tap\fR steps that carry the
target view (see \fBSTEP FILES\fR and \fBINPUT RECORDINGS\fR); text that the recording does not hold is typed as placeholder
characters. It goes to \fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR or to standard output.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write the step file here.
.RE
.TP
.B state
\fBstate save\fR \fIAPK NAME\fR saves the app's state, \fBstate load\fR \fIAPK NAME\fR puts it back.
Under ATL that is a copy of the app's data directory ($ANDROID_APP_DATA_DIR, else
$XDG_DATA_HOME/android_translation_layer, for a Flatpak launcher ~/.var/app/\fIID\fR/data/android_translation_layer;
the directory is \fIapk name\fR_), kept in $XDG_DATA_HOME/atl\-doctor/state.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-android
On the Android emulator: an AVD snapshot named atl\-doctor\-\fIPACKAGE\fR\-\fINAME\fR (adb emu avd snapshot), so
this needs an emulator. Where the emulator skips the snapshot (for example after an app used Vulkan), the
app's /data/data directory is copied as root instead (adb root) and loaded from that copy.
.TP
.BI \-\-launcher " CMD"
The ATL launcher; a Flatpak keeps the app data below ~/.var/app.
.RE
.SH STEP FILES
One command per line or separated by semicolons; \fB#\fR starts a comment outside quotes.
.PP
.nf
wait\-window "Title" [TIMEOUT]
click "Text" | click id/NAME | click X,Y     (dp, relative to android:id/content)
click X,Y android=X,Y (on Android the second point: a target laid out elsewhere there)
tap|long\-tap [id/NAME] ["Text"] [path:0/2/1] [rect:L,T,R,B]
key NAME[+NAME]       type "text"       scroll N       scroll\-smooth DY
wait SECONDS          wait\-idle [TIMEOUT]
mark ["name"]         screenshot "name"
repeat N { ... }      (also over several lines, nested)
.fi
.PP
\fBscroll\fR N sends N single mouse\-wheel notches (N > 0 down, N < 0 up), the way a real wheel does
(wl_pointer axis source wheel with value120). Under ATL this needs the preload library
\fIlibatl_doctor_wheel.so\fR, which \fBrecord\fR puts into the app by itself when it runs headless; without it
GTK sees the notches as smooth scrolling. \fBscroll\-smooth\fR DY scrolls touchpad\-like by DY units
(surface pixels under ATL, dp on Android) and is what \fBscroll\fR sent before. On Android every notch is one
swipe of 64 dp (adb cannot send a wheel source).
.PP
.PP
\fBtap\fR and \fBlong\-tap\fR (written by \fBscenario\-from\fR) look their view up in a fresh view tree by resource id, then by text
or description (also the first text below a view without text), then by the child index path from android:id/content,
and click its centre. If none is found the step does not stop the run: it clicks the centre of the rectangle (dp) if there
is one, and the report says \fBnot found\fR for this step. Each tap, click, key, type and scroll step also writes a row to
\fIreplay.jsonl\fR (target found or not, by which key, view tree taken after the step).
.PP
\fBtype\fR under ATL types through the US keyboard layout of the headless session: characters that layout has
no key for (umlauts, for example) and characters outside the Basic Multilingual Plane (emoji) cannot be typed
and fail the step.
.PP
A step file may begin with \fBstart_state:\fR \fINAME\fR: \fBrecord\fR (and \fBcompare\fR) first loads the
state saved with \fBstate save\fR, under ATL and on Android.
.PP
The same file runs under ATL and on Android, so the two recordings can be compared step by step.
Error messages carry file name and line number.
.SH INPUT RECORDINGS
\fIinput.jsonl\fR in a capture directory: line 1 is a header (\fBformat\fR 1, \fBside\fR, \fBpackage\fR, \fBfull\fR, \fBsource\fR), every
further line one event with \fBseq\fR, \fBt_us\fR (CLOCK_BOOTTIME of the marks), \fBkind\fR (tap, long\-tap, text, key, scroll, back),
\fBactivity\fR, \fBtarget\fR (\fBid\fR full resource name, \fBcls\fR, \fBtext\fR, \fBdesc\fR, \fBpath\fR child indices below
android:id/content, \fBrect\fR dp), \fBpoint\fR, and for text \fBtext\fR {\fBlen\fR}, for key \fBkey\fR, for scroll \fBscroll\fR {\fBdx\fR, \fBdy\fR}.
Typed text is not stored, only its length; the text of an EditText is left out of the target. Only a recording with
\fBfull\fR true holds the characters. Under ATL the file is written from the agent's click lines (\fBT\fR) and
\fBActivity.onBackPressed\fR; on Android \fBrecord \-\-android \-\-input\fR writes it from \fBgetevent\fR and \fBuiautomator dump\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ATL_DOCTOR_PREFIX
ATL installation prefix; replaced by \fB\-\-prefix\fR.
.TP
.B ATL_DOCTOR_ATL_SRC
ATL source tree; replaced by \fB\-\-atl\-src\fR.
.TP
.B ATL_DOCTOR_AOSP
AOSP source tree; replaced by \fB\-\-aosp\fR.
.TP
.B ATL_DOCTOR_AOSP_URL
Git URL (or path) of platform/frameworks/base to fetch AOSP source from (default: android.googlesource.com).
.TP
.B ATL_DOCTOR_AGENT
JVMTI agent library; replaced by \fB\-\-agent\fR.
.PP
Options win over environment variables. There is no configuration file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (unreadable input, a step failed, ...).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
A prerequisite that was asked for explicitly is missing (for example \fB\-\-android\fR without a device).
.TP
.B 4
.B report
or
.B diff
found findings of a class requested with \fB\-\-fail\-on\fR.
.SH FILES
A capture directory holds:
.TP
.I manifest.json
Format version, APK, command line, probes, start and end.
.TP
.I marks.tsv
Phase marks (index, boot time, wall time, name).
.TP
.I agent.tsv
JVMTI agent events: exceptions, frame times, hangs, garbage collections, heap.
.TP
.I atl.log
The app's log lines.
.TP
.I trace/
Method trace counters and the stub list.
.TP
.I trees/
View trees, one per mark.
.TP
.I shots/
Screenshots, one per mark.
.TP
.I steps.log
.TQ
.I steps.tsv
The steps that ran, and the figures per step.
.TP
.I replay.jsonl
Per input step of a step file: target found or not, by which key, and the view tree file taken after it.
\fBreport\fR \fIDIR ANDROID\-DIR\fR compares the two sides in the section \fBReplayed input\fR.
.TP
.I input.jsonl
The recorded input (see \fBINPUT RECORDINGS\fR).
.TP
.I memory.tsv
Memory per phase.
.PP
Reports are written to standard output or to the file named by \fB\-o\fR.
